<title>USA: New Mexico 350 MW coal-fired unit rumored off-line.</title>
<headline>New Mexico 350 MW coal-fired unit rumored off-line.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 350 megawatt (MW) unit 2 at the San Juan coal-fired power plant in New Mexico was taken off-line Sunday because of a boiler tube leak, market sources said Monday.</p>
<p>Official confirmation of the unit's status was not available, but industry sources said it was expected to be restarted Tuesday or Wednesday.</p>
<p>The San Juan plant, which consists of second 350 MW unit and two 540 MW units, is operated by Public Service Co of New Mexico.</p>
<p>--D Beasley, Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
